# Days of Miracles and Wonder - 2026 Update
After Paul Simon - The Boy in the Bubble (Graceland, 1986) - original line: "These are the days of miracles and wonder"
Date: 2026-09-30
Format: one stanza per line

These are the days of miracles and wonder / And don't cry baby, don't cry, don't cry
It was a slow day / And the feed was beating / On the scrollers in the checkout line / There was a rocket / Landing backwards in Texas / While a chatbot wrote a lullaby
These are the days of miracles and wonder / This is the long-distance call / The way the camera follows us in slo-mo / The way we look to us all
We got telescopes seeing first light / Baby pictures from the edge of time / We got CRISPR scissors rewriting code / And mRNA in record time / We got taxis with no drivers in Phoenix / Real-time translation on a phone / Fusion flashing twice in Livermore / And black holes photographed - unknown, now known
It was a slow day / And the grid was humming / On the solar roofs in the summer heat / There was a robot / Folding proteins in seconds / What took grad students years to complete
These are the days of miracles and wonder / This is the late-night lab report / The way the model dreams in language / The way we teach it, short and short
We got dishes talking to the far side / Startup landers bouncing on the Moon / We got midnight launches out of Mahia / We got rain maps made by balloon / We got voices cloned from three seconds / We got fake and real in the same frame / We got cures for sickle cell approved / And the climate models calling names
These are the days of lasers in the data center / Lights that stitch the world to all / Staccato signals of constant information / And your phone says "baby, don't cry, don't cry" / These are the days of miracles and wonder / Don't cry baby, don't cry, don't cry
